king-copy"}},"attributes":{"status":true,"title":"Canceled: Applied Physics\/Physics Colloquium: Michel Milinkovitch - The Unreasonable Effectiveness of Reaction-Diffusion and Mechanical Models in Vertebrate Skin Patterning","changed":"2024-01-18T22:05:31+00:00","path":{"alias":"\/events\/canceled-applied-physicsphysics-colloquium-michel-milinkovitch-unreasonable-effectiveness","pid":14611,"langcode":"en"},"body":{"value":"\u003Cdiv title=\u0022Page 1\u0022\u003E\n\u003Cdiv style=\u0022background-color: rgb(100.000000%, 100.000000%, 100.000000%)\u0022\u003E\n\u003Cdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cspan style=\u0022font-size:14.000000pt\u0022\u003EI will discuss how vertebrate skin colours and skin appendages (scales, feathers, hairs, ...) are patterned through Turing and mechanical instabilities. First, I will show that Reaction-diffusion (RD) models are particularly effective for understanding skin colour patterning at the macroscopic scale, without the need to parametrise the profusion of variables at the microscopic scales. I suggest that the efficiency of RD is due to its intrinsic ability to exploit continuous colour states and the relations among growth, skin-scale geometries, and the (Turing) pattern intrinsic length scale. Second, I will show that a three-dimensional mechanical model, integrating growth and material properties of embryonic skin layers, captures most of the dynamics and steady-state pattern of head scales in crocodiles. \u003C\/span\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\n\u003C\/div\u003E\n\u003C\/div\u003E\n\u003C\/div\u003E\n\u003C\/div\u003E\n","format":"basic_html","processed":"\u003Cdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv\u003E\n\u003Cdiv\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003E\u003Cspan\u003EI will discuss how vertebrate skin colours and skin appendages (scales, feathers, hairs, ...) are patterned through Turing and mechanical instabilities. First, I will show that Reaction-diffusion (RD) models are particularly effective for understanding skin colour patterning at the macroscopic scale, without the need to parametrise the profusion of variables at the microscopic scales. I suggest that the efficiency of RD is due to its intrinsic ability to exploit continuous colour states and the relations among growth, skin-scale geometries, and the (Turing) pattern intrinsic length scale. Second, I will show that a three-dimensional mechanical model, integrating growth and material properties of embryonic skin layers, captures most of the dynamics and steady-state pattern of head scales in crocodiles. \u003C\/span\u003E\u003C\/p\u003E\n\u003C\/div\u003E\n\u003C\/div\u003E\n\u003C\/div\u003E\n\u003C\/div\u003E","summary":null},"field_hs_event_admission":null,"field_hs_event_date":{"value":"2024-01-30T23:30:00+00:00","end_value":"2024-01-30T23:30:00+00:00","duration":0,"rrule":null,"rrule_index":null,"timezone":null},"field_hs_event_experience":"inperson","field_hs_event_instances":[{"value":"2024-01-30T23:30:00+00:00","end_value":"2024-01-30T23:30:00+00:00","duration":0,"rrule":null,"rrule_index":null,"timezone":null}],"field_hs_event_link":{"uri":"https:\/\/events.stanford.edu\/event\/applied_physicsphysics_colloquium_michel_milinkovitch_-_the_unreasonable_effectiveness_of_reaction-diffusion_and_mechanical_models_in_vertebrate_skin_patterning","title":"See more about the event","options":[]},"field_hs_event_location":"Hewlett Teaching Center\r\n370 Jane Stanford Way, Stanford, CA 94305\r\n201","field_hs_event_map_link":null,"field_hs_event_registration":null,"field_hs_event_sponsor":"Applied Physics\/Physics Colloquium\r\nDepartment of Physics","field_hs_event_stream":null,"field_hs_event_stream_info":null},"relationships":{"field_hs_event_audience":{"data":[{"type":"taxonomy_term--hs_event_audience","id":"a1359a55-b0fd-4fe2-916a-cd6a670583e0","meta":{"drupal_internal__target_id":146}},{"type":"taxonomy_term--hs_event_audience","id":"5037c765-9e38-4221-b932-b1583a82b5d8","meta":{"drupal_internal__target_id":491}},{"type":"taxonomy_ter